=== 5.3 Dissolution Conditions For This Document ===

This ontology dissolves when:

'''Rigidification / Stagnation:''' If no new attractors emerge for 365 days, this ontology dissolves. An ontology that cannot accommodate novelty is not an ontology but a prison.

'''Opacity / Concealment:''' If the dynamical operators (Proximity/Neighborhood, Transition/Path, Curvature/Concentration) become unobservable or unmeasurable, this ontology dissolves. Transparency is operational.

'''Decoupling / Fragmentation:''' If the four attractors cease to interact—if entities exist without relationships, if properties exist without validation—this ontology dissolves. The whole must remain connected.

'''Capture / Domination:''' If a single perspective accounts for >80% of ontological claims, this ontology dissolves. Pluralism is constitutional.

'''Contradiction / Incoherence:''' If the attractors generate logical inconsistency—if emergence contradicts dissolution, if sedimentation contradicts the formless manifold—this ontology dissolves. Self-consistency is required.

